[2026-11-16T09:18:28.686Z] [design-st-2c7624] [request] Observation: {"ok":true,"sections":[{"label":"--- xcoder-ai-dojo/dojo-blueprint.md (lines 90-175 of 386) ---","content":"         ├─ SdlcRun → external Node agent CLI\n         └─ voice controller → recognition / synthesis workers\n\nLocal state: ~/.xcoder/dojo\nExternal systems: configured LLM, optional online TTS, package/model sources,\n                  user-selected APIs, SSH hosts, Docker engine, network targets\n```\n\nThe GUI coordinates work through Qt signals and `QProcess`. The executable also acts as a worker host, allowing the packaged application to start its own API, process, recognition, and synthesis modes without relying on a separately installed Python interpreter.\n\nThe shared developer console admits one process at a time. This is distinct from the AI task scheduler, which supports up to four model requests across workspaces and one active request per workspace. JARVIS maintains its own process and busy state; these are not one unified scheduler.\n\n### Module map\n\n| Module | Responsibility |\n| --- | --- |\n| `__init__.py`, `VERSION`, `__main__.py` | Version identity and module entry point |\n| `main.py` | Startup, worker dispatch, main window, file lifecycle, console integration |\n| `editor.py` | Text editing, syntax highlighting, line numbers, source extraction |\n| `markdown_preview.py` | Debounced Markdown rendering and local image resolution |\n| `runners.py` | Project discovery, runtime selection, command representation, process host, SQLite |\n| `tool_commands.py` | Developer-tool presets, shell/network/SSH command construction |\n| `tool_panels.py` | Tool controls, API collection storage, agent catalog panel |\n| `curl_import.py`, `api_request.py` | cURL parsing and HTTP/model worker |\n| `preferences.py` | Persistent preferences, LLM configuration, settings UI, request construction |\n| `assistant.py` | Persistent AI task board, scheduling, controls, conversation context |\n| `assistant_storage.py` | Windows account-bound protection for stored assistant text |\n| `jarvis.py` | Interactive assistant, chat memory, voice UI, tool dispatch and delegation |\n| `workspace_tools.py` | Bounded workspace reads, search, Python inspection and Git inspection |\n| `sdlc_tool.py` | External agent discovery, installation commands, launch, output and stopping |\n| `agent_tools.py` | Pinned Docker-oriented catalog and engine health command |\n| `voice.py`, `voice_input.py` | Audio lifecycle, capture, playback and recognition coordination |\n| `speech_worker.py`, `tts_worker.py` | Recognition and synthesis worker entry points |\n| `voice_options.py`, `voice_settings.py` | Voice presets, saved options and configuration controls |\n| `theme.py`, `hub.py`, `hud_controls.py`, `hud_presets.py` | Themes, artwork, hub and HUD presentation |\n| `data_paths.py` | Canonical data directory and non-destructive legacy migration |\n\n## 5. Workspace, editor, and execution design\n\n### Workspace and files\n\nA workspace is a filesystem directory. The active file and selected folder provide context for project discovery and tool panels; panels also allow an explicit working-folder override. Command-line paths can select an initial folder and files. Without paths, startup uses the current working directory.\n\nNew files use UTF-8. New Windows PowerShell files include a UTF-8 BOM. Existing UTF-8 BOMs and line-ending conventions are preserved, and Python source encodings are supported. Unsaved changes participate in the close/save flow. Running saves the active file; other edited tabs should be saved before project execution.\n\n### Runtime matrix\n\n| Input | Resolution/execution |\n| --- | --- |\n| Python | Closest suitable workspace `.venv`, otherwise an available Python interpreter; frozen app uses external project Python |\n| JavaScript | Node.js for `.js`, `.mjs`, `.cjs` |\n| TypeScript | Local `tsx` where available; otherwise Node's supported type-stripping path |\n| React / Vue / npm | Recognized package scripts: `dev`, `start`, or 
