[2026-11-16T09:20:26.146Z] [design-st-2c7624] [stop=end_turn] [response] <｜｜DSML｜｜ calls>\n<｜｜DSML｜｜ invoke name="edit_file">\n<｜｜DSML｜｜ parameter name="input" string="false">{"path": ".xcoder/backlog/design-st-2c7624.md", "old_str": "<!-- APPEND-HERE -->", "new_str": "---\n\n## 11. P-07 Approval Sheet (modal)\n\n**Purpose:** the single human-in-the-loop gate for high-impact actions. Two kinds only: `file-write` and `delegation-launch`. Anything destructive or out-of-workspace is refused outright and never appears here for approval [S-07, AI-03].\n\n**Data requirements**\n\n| Field | Source | Type | Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| approvalId | approval request | string | single-use, bound to the originating toolCallId |\n| kind | request | `'file-write' \\| 'delegation-launch'` | nothing else is approvable |\n| concreteTarget | request | string | absolute-normalized relPath, or CLI + task summary |\n| diffSummary | main (file-write only) | `{added, removed, preview}` | sanitized preview, no secrets |\n| expiresAtMs | request | number | expired → `approval-expired` |\n| requestedBy | request | `'agent'` | user-initiated saves do not prompt |\n\n```ts\nexport type ApprovalKind = 'file-write' | 'delegation-launch';\nexport type ApprovalDecision = 'approve-once' | 'deny';\nexport interface ApprovalRequest {\n  approvalId: string;\n  kind: ApprovalKind;\n  toolCallId: string;\n  concreteTarget: string;                 // MUST be shown verbatim in the sheet\n  detail:\n    | { kind: 'file-write'; relPath: string; bytes: number; diffSummary: { added: number; removed: number; preview: string } }\n    | { kind: 'delegation-launch'; cliLabel: string; taskSummary: string };\n  requestedAtMs: number;\n  expiresAtMs: number;\n  status: 'pending' | 'approved' | 'denied' | 'expired';\n}\nexport interface ApprovalResponseRequest { approvalId: string; decision: ApprovalDecision; }\nexport interface ApprovalModel { queue: ReadonlyArray<ApprovalRequest>; active: ApprovalRequest | null; }\nexport interface ApprovalActions {\n  respond(request: ApprovalResponseRequest): Promise<ApprovalRequest>;  // approval.respond\n  dismiss(): void;                                                     // = deny, explicitly\n}\n```\n\n**Display modes:** detail only (one request at a time; the queue is shown as a count). **States:** pending, approved (sheet closes; originating card updates), denied (card shows `denied-approval`, audited), expired (target changed on disk → re-request, never auto-approve).\n**Security:** the target is named concretely and verbatim — no \"approve this action?\" without a target [AC-15]; dismissal counts as deny; decisions are audited with the decision and the request id, never with file contents; there is no \"remember my choice\" for these two kinds [CORE-05 fail closed, AI-03].\n\n---\n\n## 12. P-08 Settings (P-08a / P-08b / P-08c)\n\n**Purpose:** configure the model, the limits, the secret, and the cosmetics — and disclose where data lives.\n\n**Data requirements**\n\n| Field | Source | Type | Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| provider / baseUrl / modelName | `settings.get` | string | base URL shown shortened; no credentials in it |\n| hasApiKey | `settings.get` | boolean | **the key itself is never returned** [UI-07, S-02] |\n| limits | `settings.get` | `{maxContextChars, maxOutputTokens, maxTurns, maxRequestsPerSession}` | displayed, editable within bounds |\n| dataRootDisplay / auditLogDir / retentionDays | `audit.location` | string / number | disclosed [AC-18, S-11] |\n| delegationCliLabel | settings | string | the AC-13 default CLI, user-overridable |\n| appearance | settings | `'dark' \\| 'light' \\| 'system'` | no artwork parity claim (NG-07) |\n\n```ts\nexport interface LlmSettingsView {\n  provider: 'openai-compatible' | 'none';\n  baseUrlLabel: string;\n  modelName: string;\n  [REDACTED];                     // write-only secret; no read path exists\n  limits: AgentLimits;\n  delegationCliLabel: string;\n  dataRootDisplay: string;\n  auditLogDir: string;\n  auditRetentionDays: number;\n}\nexport interface AgentLimits {\n  maxContextChars: number;   // default 12000-equivalent budget\n  [REDACTED];\n  maxTurns: number;          // default 6\n  maxRequestsPerSession: number;\n}\nexport interface LlmSettingsPatch {\n  provider?: 'openai-compatible' | 'none';\n  baseUrl?: string;          // validated as http(s), no embedded creds\n  modelName?: string;\n  limits?: Partial<AgentLimits>;\n  delegationCliLabel?: string;\n  appearance?: 'dark' | 'light' | 'system';\n}\nexport interface ApiKeyInput { value: string; }   // write-only; field autocomplete off, cleared on submit\nexport interface SettingsModel { view: LlmSettingsView; draft: LlmSettingsPatch; dirty: boolean; saving: boolean; }\nexport interface SettingsActions {\n  get(): Promise<LlmSettingsView>;                     // settings.get\n  update(patch: LlmSettingsPatch): Promise<LlmSettingsView>;\n  setApiKey(input: ApiKeyInput): Promise<LlmSettingsView>;\n  clearApiKey(): Promise<LlmSettingsView>;\n  testConnection(): Promise<{ ok: boolean; error?: AppError }>;\n  openDataRoot(): Promise<void>;                       // OS reveal\n  openAuditLog(): void;                                // P-10\n}\n```\n\n**Display modes:** detail (form), editable (except the key, which is write-only and shows `•••• set` / `not set`). **States:** unconfigured, configured, saving, validation error (inline per field), connection test failing (message, not a stack).\n**Security:** key is stored in the OS-protected store via main only, never in the renderer, URL, logs or prompts [CORE-07, UI-07, CORE-01]; the key field has autocomplete off and is cleared on submit and on modal close [UI-10]; limits are bounded in main so a renderer cannot raise them past policy [S-10]; changing the provider clears the in-memory key reference.\n\n---\n\n## 13. P-09 Conversation History\n\n**Purpose:** browse, restore and clear persisted conversations [AC-17].\n\n**Data requirements**\n\n| Field | Source | Type |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| sessions | `session.list` | `SessionSummary[]` (cursor-paginated) |\n| sessionId / title / updatedAtMs / workspaceId / entryCount | main | — |\n| loaded detail | `session.load` | `SessionDetail` (paged transcript) |\n\n```ts\nexport interface SessionSummary {\n  sessionId: string; title: string; updatedAtMs: number; entryCount: number;\n  workspaceName: string | null;   // name only, not the full path\n}\nexport interface SessionDetail { sessionId: string; entries: TranscriptEntry[]; nextCursor: string | null; }\nexport interface HistoryModel { sessions: ReadonlyArray<SessionSummary>; nextCursor: string | null; selectedSessionId: string | null; loading: boolean; }\nexport interface HistoryActions {\n  list(): Promise<SessionSummary[]>;\n  load(sessionId: string): Promise<SessionDetail>;\n  resume(sessionId: string): Promise<void>;    // loads into P-05\n  clear(sessionId: string): Promise<void>;     // irreversible, confirmed\n  clearAll(): Promise<void>;                   // irreversible, confirmed twice\n}\n```\n\n**Display modes:** list (sessions, sortable by updatedAt, searchable by title, paginated), detail (transcript preview), editable only in the sense of delete. **States:** empty, loading, cleared (removal confirmed by re-list).\n**Security:** session titles derive from the first user turn and are rendered escaped; no tool results are stored beyond the redacted summaries the transcript already shows [S-11]; clearing removes the record, not just the view.\n\n---\n\n## 14. P-10 Audit Log Viewer + P-11 Status Bar + P-12 Error Center\n\n### P-10 Audit Log Viewer (modal)\n\n**Purpose:** read-only inspection of the redacted, retention-capped audit log whose location is disclosed in P-08b/P-11 [S-11, CORE-08].\n\n```ts\nexport type AuditEventType =\n  | 'workspace-open' | 'workspace-close' | 'file-save' | 'run-start' | 'run-stop'\n  | 'agent-request' | 'agent-response' | 'tool-call' | 'tool-refusal'\n  | 'delegation-start' | 'delegation-stop' | 'approval-request' | 'approval-decision'\n  | 'settings-change' | 'secret-set' | 'secret-cleared' | 'error';\nexport interface AuditEventView {\n  eventId: string; atMs: number; type: AuditEventType;\n  actor: 'user' | 'agent' | 'system';\n  targetRelPath?: string;\n  toolName?: AllowlistedToolName;   // never for non-tool events\n  outcome: 'ok' | 'refused' | 'denied' | 'failed';\n  redactedSummary: string;          // pre-redacted in main; no secrets, no PII, no file bodies\n}\nexport interface AuditPageRequest { cursor?: string; limit?: number; type?: AuditEventType; sinceMs?: number; }\nexport interface AuditPage { events: AuditEventView[]; nextCursor: string | null; retentionDays: number; }\nexport interface AuditModel { events: ReadonlyArray<AuditEventView>; nextCursor: string | null; filterType: AuditEventType | null; retentionDays: number; }\nexport interface AuditActions {\n  page(request: AuditPageRequest): Promise<AuditPage>;\n  location(): Promise<{ logDir: string; retentionDays: number }>;\n  exportRedacted(): Promise<{ path: string }>;   // redacted copy only, to a user-chosen path\n}\n```\n\n**Display modes:** list (cursor-paginated, sortable by time, filterable by type), detail (single event drawer), read-only — no editing, no deleting from the UI.\n**Security:** the viewer is tamper-evident in the sense that it is append-only from the app's side; it never renders un-redacted content; export produces a redacted file only.\n\n### P-11 Status Bar\n\n```ts\nexport interface StatusBarModel {\n  workspacePathDisplay: string | null;   // always visible when open\n  run: { state: RunState; label: string };\n  agent: { state: AgentRequestState; label: string };\n  model: { state: 'configured' | 'missing' | 'error'; label: string };\n  audit: { logDir: string; retentionDays: number };  // clickable -> P-10\n  selection: { relPath: string; language: SupportedLanguage } | null;\n}\nexport interface StatusBarActions {\n  openAuditLog(): void;\n  openRunConsole(): void;\n  openAgentPanel(): void;\n  openSettings(): void;\n}\n```\n\n**Display modes:** view only; three-state badges; the audit-log location is always one click away [S-11 disclosure].\n\n### P-12 Error Center\n\n```ts\nexport interface ErrorToast { toastId: string; error: AppError; atMs: number; dismissed: boolean; }\nexport interface ErrorCenterModel { toasts: ReadonlyArray<ErrorToast>; detailOpenFor: string | null; }\nexport interface ErrorCenterActions {\n  dismiss(toastId: string): void;\n  openDetail(toastId: string): void;\n  retry(toastId: string): Promise<void>;   // only for retryable codes\n}\n```\n\n**Display modes:** list (toast stack, time-ordered, auto-dismiss only for informational codes), detail (sheet with remediation). **Rules:** errors never block the whole window except for fatal renderer failure; messages are pre-redacted; stacks and provider payloads go to the audit log detail ref, not the toast.\n\n<!-- APPEND-HERE -->\n"}</｜｜DSML｜｜ parameter>\n</｜｜DSML｜｜ invoke>\n</｜｜DSML｜｜ calls>
