[2026-11-16T09:20:54.696Z] [design-st-2c7624] [stop=end_turn] [response] <｜｜DSML｜｜ calls>\n<｜｜DSML｜｜ invoke name="edit_file">\n<｜｜DSML｜｜ parameter name="input" string="false">{"path": ".xcoder/backlog/design-st-2c7624.md", "old_str": "<!-- APPEND-HERE -->", "new_str": "---\n\n## 15. Tradeoffs (explicit, with cost)\n\nEach tradeoff names what was gained and what was given up, so a reviewer can overturn it knowingly.\n\n- **T-01 Single-flight console vs. concurrent runs** — *Chosen:* one run at a time; a second request returns `run-busy`, no queue. *Gained:* a simple, auditable execution contract, one Stop target, no scheduler state machine. *Cost:* a user cannot watch two projects run at once, and cannot queue a run. *Why acceptable:* matches the reference's shared console and keeps AC-06/AC-07 verifiable; queueing is additive later.\n- **T-02 Page-level spec instead of component-level** — *Chosen:* specify pages/subpages (P-xx) with page models, not every React component. *Gained:* contracts stay stable when implementation refactors components; the design survives framework churn. *Cost:* implementation freedom inside a page can drift from the intended UX unless the page's action contract is respected.\n- **T-03 Approval only for two action classes** — *Chosen:* exactly `file-write` and `delegation-launch` prompt; everything else is either harmless-read or refused outright. *Gained:* no approval fatigue, and no path to approve a dangerous action. *Cost:* if a new high-impact action is added later it must be classified explicitly or it silently has no gate — mitigated by making `requiresApproval` a required field on every `ActionDescriptor`.\n- **T-04 No free-text workspace path input** — *Chosen:* workspace opening happens only through the OS dialog or a re-validated recents entry. *Gained:* removes an entire unvalidated path-input surface and its traversal/credential edge cases [S-06]. *Cost:* power users cannot paste a path; they must use the dialog. Accepted for v1.\n- **T-05 Tree filtering in main, filter-in-renderer only over loaded nodes** — *Chosen:* exclusions (dotfiles, generated dirs, credential names) are decided in main and excluded nodes are never sent; the user's text filter applies only to already-loaded children. *Gained:* the sandbox decision has exactly one implementation [PRM-09]; no client-side filter can be bypassed. *Cost:* filtering is not a full-workspace search, and a filtered tree can look incomplete — surfaced by naming the bounds in the empty/truncated states.\n- **T-06 Read caps visible rather than silent** — *Chosen:* when a read hits the char/line/file bound, the UI shows `truncated` + counts. *Gained:* the user is never shown a partial file as if it were complete [AC-19]. *Cost:* more UI states, and a truncated buffer is deliberately not silently saveable as complete.\n- **T-07 Markdown preview blocks HTML and remote images visibly** — *Chosen:* sanitized AST only, local images only, with a visible \"blocked\" count. *Gained:* closes the main XSS/SSRF/surveillance-image vector in a preview pane [UI-02/UI-03, AC-20]. *Cost:* some legitimate Markdown renders incompletely; the annotation keeps that honest rather than confusing.\n- **T-08 Transcript is append-only, not editable** — *Chosen:* users can copy and clear, not edit prior turns. *Gained:* the transcript stays a trustworthy audit artifact and matches the redacted-log requirement. *Cost:* fixing a typo mid-conversation requires a new turn; no in-place editing or branching.\n- **T-09 Settings as a modal, not a route** — *Chosen:* Settings/History/Audit are overlays over the workbench rather than pages that replace it. *Gained:* the workspace, run and agent state stay mounted and never restart because of navigation; simpler state ownership. *Cost:* deep-linking to a settings tab is not possible; overlay stack management is required.\n- **T-10 Agent output labelled and escaped, never rendered as rich UI** — *Chosen:* model text renders escaped with sanitized markdown and an AI-generated label; tool calls render as structured cards produced by main, not by the model. *Gained:* a prompt injection cannot forge a real tool card or executable UI [UI-13, PRM-01/08]. *Cost:* richer presentational answers (tables, embeds) are not supported; everything is text + cards.\n\n---\n\n## 16. Action -> page -> enforcement matrix\n\n| Action | Page(s) | Side effect | Approval | Enforced/validated in | Primary ACs |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `workspace.open` | P-01, P-00 | read | no | main (dialog + root confinement) | AC-01, AC-02 |\n| `workspace.close` | P-00 | none | no | main (unsaved prompt) | AC-03 |\n| `tree.listChildren` | P-02 | read | no | main (sandbox, bounds) | AC-02, AC-11 |\n| `file.open` | P-02, P-03 | read | no | main (encoding/kind detection) | AC-03, AC-05 |\n| `file.save` | P-03 | write | **only if agent-initiated** | main (encoding/EOL, baseSha) | AC-04, AC-15 |\n| `file.revert` | P-03 | write | no (user-initiated, discards buffer) | renderer + main | AC-03 |\n| `run.resolveTargets` | P-04, P-04a | read | no | main (target allowlist) | AC-06, AC-08 |\n| `run.start` | P-04 | execute | no (user-initiated) | main (argv, cwd, timeout, single-flight) | AC-06, AC-07, AC-08 |\n| `run.stop` | P-04 | execute | no | main (terminate + escalation) | AC-07 |\n| `agent.send` | P-05 | read + external | no | main (limits, tool allowlist, prompt assembly) | AC-09, AC-10, AC-19 |\n| `agent.stop` | P-05 | none | no | main (abort in-flight) | AC-09 |\n| `delegation.launch` | P-06 (via P-07) | execute | **yes** | main (requires consumed approvalId) | AC-13, AC-15 |\n| `delegation.stop` | P-06 | execute | no | main | AC-13 |\n| `approval.respond` | P-07 | none | n/a | main (single-use, expiry) | AC-15 |\n| `settings.setApiKey` / `clearApiKey` | P-08a/b | secret | no | main + OS key store (never returned) | AC-18 |\n| `session.clear` | P-05, P-09 | write | no (explicit confirm) | main | AC-17 |\n| `audit.page` / `audit.location` | P-10, P-11 | read | no | main (redaction, retention) | AC-18, S-11 |\n\nNote the two actions that touch writes/execution from the agent side are the only ones carrying `requiresApproval: true`; both are also unreachable by a model without a matching, unexpired `approvalId`.\n\n---\n\n## 17. Component -> interface coverage (AC1)\n\n| Component | Page ID | Interface(s) defined | Display modes |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| App Shell | P-00 | `ShellModel`, `ShellActions`, `DojoBridge` | view |\n| Welcome | P-01 | `WelcomeModel`, `WelcomeActions` | list, view |\n| Workspace Explorer | P-02 | `FileNode`, `TreeNodePage`, `ExplorerModel`, `ExplorerActions` | list, sort, filter, lazy-page |\n| Node Context Menu | P-02a | `NodeContextMenuModel` | detail |\n| Editor Area | P-03 | `EditorTabState`, `EditorModel`, `EditorActions` | editable, detail |\n| Text Editor Pane | P-03a | `FileReadResult`, `EditorActions` | editable |\n| Markdown Preview | P-03b | `MarkdownPreviewModel` | view (read-only) |\n| Unopenable File | P-03c | `FileOpenErrorCode`, `EditorTabState` | detail (error) |\n| Run Console | P-04 | `RunTarget`, `RunSession`, `ConsoleModel`, `ConsoleActions` | view, list, filter, search |\n| Run Target Picker | P-04a | `RunTarget`, `ConsoleActions.resolveTargets` | list (single select) |\n| Agent Panel | P-05 | `TranscriptEntry`, `AgentModel`, `AgentActions`, `AgentEvent` | view, list, search, paged |\n| Tool Call Card | P-05a | `ToolCallRecord`, `AllowlistedToolName` | detail |\n| Turn-Limit Banner | P-05b | `AgentModel.request` | detail (terminal) |\n| Model-Not-Configured | P-05c | `AgentModel.modelState`, `LlmSettingsView` | detail (empty) |\n| Delegation Run View | P-06 | `DelegationRun`, `DelegationModel`, `DelegationActions` | view, list, search |\n| Approval Sheet | P-07 | `ApprovalRequest`, `ApprovalModel`, `ApprovalActions` | detail |\n| Settings | P-08 | `LlmSettingsView`, `LlmSettingsPatch`, `SettingsActions` | detail, editable |\n| Model & Limits | P-08a | `AgentLimits`, `SettingsActions` | editable |\n| Data, Secrets & Audit | P-08b | `ApiKeyInput`, `LlmSettingsView` | editable (key write-only) |\n| Appearance | P-08c | `LlmSettingsPatch.appearance` | editable |\n| Conversation History | P-09 | `SessionSummary`, `SessionDetail`, `HistoryActions` | list, sort, search, paged |\n| Audit Log Viewer | P-10 | `AuditEventView`, `AuditPage`, `AuditActions` | list, sort, filter, paged |\n| Status Bar | P-11 | `StatusBarModel`, `StatusBarActions` | view |\n| Error Center | P-12 | `AppError`, `ErrorCenterModel`, `ErrorCenterActions` | list, detail |\n\nEvery component named above has at least one exported interface for its data and one for its actions (or an explicitly inherited one), which is the AC1 evidence.\n\n---\n\n## 18. AC traceability (UI-level)\n\n| AC | How this design satisfies it |\n| --- | --- |\n| AC-01 | P-00 title bar renders `Xcoder Dojo` + workspace path; P-11 mirrors it |\n| AC-02 | P-02 lazy `listChildren` per directory; nothing above root is requestable |\n| AC-03 | P-03 tabs with CodeMirror highlighting, line numbers, close, dirty dot |\n| AC-04 | P-03 save carries `encoding`/`eol` from `FileReadResult`; new files default UTF-8 |\n| AC-05 | P-03c with `binary-file`/`not-utf8` + \"nothing modified\" copy |\n| AC-06 | P-04 saves active file first, streams stdout/stderr, shows exit code |\n| AC-07 | P-04 single-flight + `stopping` state + stopped-reported exit path |\n| AC-08 | P-04 `runtime-missing` and non-zero exit bars |\n| AC-09 | P-05 `AgentEvent.tool-call` -> P-05a card with args, outcome, duration |\n| AC-10 | P-05 `turn-progress` + P-05b terminal turn-limit banner |\n| AC-11 | P-05a `refused-sandbox`/`refused-credential` outcomes; no content in card |\n| AC-12 | P-05 delimited `workspace-data` entries; `tool-not-allowlisted` rejection notice |\n| AC-13 | P-06 streamed output, working Stop, `failed-workspace-changed` refusal |\n| AC-14 | P-05a git_* cards render read-only results; no stage/commit/push action exists in any interface |\n| AC-15 | P-07 `concreteTarget` verbatim + audited decision; `approval-expired` re-prompt |\n| AC-16 | P-05c plus disabled send; P-01/02/03/04 unaffected |\n| AC-17 | P-09 list/resume/clear over persisted sessions; transcript restored on start |\n| AC-18 | P-08b shows `hasApiKey` only; P-10/P-11 disclose log location |\n| AC-19 | Every capped surface carries `truncated` + counts (P-02, P-03, P-04, P-05a, P-06) |\n| AC-20 | P-03b sanitized AST, local images only, visible blocked count |\n| AC-21 | Not a UI concern; the interface shapes above are what unit tests assert against |\n\n---\n\n## 19. Open questions carried forward (design defaults)\n\n1. **Default delegation CLI** — design assumes a user-configurable label (`delegationCliLabel`) with one concrete default chosen at implementation; P-06 hides the third state behind `failed-cli-missing`.\n2. **Token-by-token streaming** — assumed yes; P-05 renders `delta` events and P-06 renders line chunks. If the implementation buffers instead, `AgentEvent.delta` collapses to `entry-completed` and P-05 loses only the streaming affordance, not its contract.\n3. **Stub model server** — assumed in-repo under `xcoder-dojo/test/`; P-05's `modelState: 'error'` path is what the UI shows when it is unreachable.\n4. **Terminal/SSH/HTTP panels** — out of scope (NG-05); P-04 is the only execution surface in this design.\n\n---\n\n## 20. Deliberate omissions from this document\n\nModule/folder layout, build commands, Electron security configuration details, prompt text and tool JSON schemas (versioned elsewhere per S-12), and the LLM request/response wire format. Those belong to the architecture and implementation stages; this document fixes only what the user can see and what each surface may ask main to do.\n"}</｜｜DSML｜｜ parameter>\n</｜｜DSML｜｜ invoke>\n</｜｜DSML｜｜ calls>
