(data), action contracts (side-effect class + approval + enforcing process), and the IPC bridge. Tradeoffs = UX richness vs. simplicity/enforceability, each with an owned cost.",\n      "navigation_hierarchy": [\n        "P-00 App Shell — persistent chrome: title bar (Xcoder Dojo + workspace path), left dock, center, right dock, bottom dock, status bar, overlay slot",\n        "P-01 Welcome / No-Workspace — center; recents list + choose-folder CTA; no free-text path field",\n        "P-02 Workspace Explorer (left dock) — lazy per-directory tree; + P-02a Node Context Menu",\n        "P-03 Editor Area (center, tabbed) — + P-03a Text Editor Pane (CodeMirror 6, highlighting, line numbers), P-03b Markdown Preview Pane, P-03c Unopenable File State",\n        "P-04 Run Console (bottom dock, single-flight) — + P-04a Run Target Picker",\n        "P-05 Agent Panel / JARVIS (right dock) — + P-05a Tool Call Card, P-05b Turn-Limit Banner, P-05c Model-Not-Configured State",\n        "P-06 Delegation Run View — right-dock takeover for the external agent CLI",\n        "P-07 Approval Sheet — modal gate for exactly file-write and delegation-launch",\n        "P-08 Settings — + P-08a Model & Limits, P-08b Data/Secrets/Audit, P-08c Appearance",\n        "P-09 Conversation History — drawer over P-05",\n        "P-10 Audit Log Viewer, P-11 Status Bar, P-12 Error Center"\n      ],\n      "shared_contracts": {\n        "AppErrorCode": "closed union (path-escape, credential-file, binary-file, not-utf8, run-busy, runtime-missing, turn-limit, tool-not-allowlisted, approval-expired, secret-detected, ...) so pages render codes, never raw stacks or provider payloads",\n        "AppError": "{ code, message (pre-redacted), remediation?, detailRef? }",\n        "ActionDescriptor<In,Out>": "{ name, sideEffect: none|read|write|execute|secret, requiresApproval: boolean, enforcedIn: 'main', validate(input), run(input) } — requiresApproval is non-optional so a new high-impact action cannot silently lack a gate",\n        "BridgeResult<T>": "{ ok: true, value } | { ok: false, error: AppError }",\n        "DojoBridge": "workspace / tree / files / run / agent / session / delegation / approval / settings / audit / errors — the entire privileged surface; preload exposes no ipcRenderer passthrough, validates every payload in main, and can never return the API key (only [REDACTED]"\n      },\n      "per_page_interface_index": {\n        "P-00": ["ShellModel", "ShellActions"],\n        "P-01": ["WelcomeModel", "WelcomeActions"],\n        "P-02 / P-02a": ["FileNode", "ListChildrenRequest", "TreeNodePage", "ExplorerModel", "ExplorerActions", "NodeContextMenuModel"],\n        "P-03 / a / b / c": ["FileOpenErrorCode", "FileReadResult", "EditorTabState", "SaveRequest", "SaveResult", "EditorModel", "EditorActions", "MarkdownSpan", "MarkdownBlock", "MarkdownPreviewModel"],\n        "P-04 / P-04a": ["RunState", "CommandSpec", "RunTarget", "RunStartRequest", "ConsoleChunk", "RunSession", "ConsoleModel", "ConsoleActions", "RunEvent"],\n        "P-05 / a / b / c": ["AgentRequestState", "AllowlistedToolName", "ToolCallOutcome", "ToolCallRecord", "TranscriptEntry", "AgentSendRequest", "AgentEvent", "AgentModel", "AgentActions"],\n        "P-06": ["DelegationState", "DelegationLaunchRequest", "DelegationChunk", "DelegationRun", "DelegationEvent", "DelegationModel", "DelegationActions"],\n        "P-07": ["ApprovalKind", "ApprovalDecision", "ApprovalRequest", "ApprovalResponseRequest", "ApprovalModel", "ApprovalActions"],\n        "P-08 / a / b / c": ["AgentLimits", "LlmSettingsView", "LlmSettingsPatch", "ApiKeyInput", "SettingsModel", "SettingsActions"],\n        "P-09": ["SessionSummary", "SessionDetail", "HistoryModel", "HistoryActions"],\n        "P-10 / P-11 / P-12": ["AuditEventType", "AuditEventView", "AuditPageRequest", "AuditPage", "AuditModel", "AuditActions", "StatusBarModel", "StatusBarActions", "ErrorToast", "ErrorCenterModel", "ErrorCenterActions"]\n      },\n      "display_modes_summary": {\n        "view_only": ["P-00", "P-03b", "P-11"],\n        "list_and_sort": ["P-01 (recency)", "P-02 (name/size/mtime)", "P-04 chunks (time-ordered, immutable)", "P-05 tool cards", "P-09 (updatedAt)", "P-10 (time)"],\n        "searchable_filterable": ["P-02 text filter over loaded nodes", "P-04 stream filter + find", "P-05 outcome filter + find", "P-06 find", "P-09 title search", "P-10 type filter"],\n        "editable": ["P-03a buffer", "P-08 forms (key is write-only)", "P-07 decision"],\n        "paginated": ["P-02 per-directory nextCursor", "P-04/P-06 ring-buffer window", "P-05 transcript lazy pages", "P-09 cursor", "P-10 cursor"],\n        "detail_only": ["P-02a", "P-03c", "P-05a", "P-05b", "P-05c", "P-07", "P-12 detail sheet"]\n      },\n      "explicit_tradeoffs": [\n        "T-01 Single-flight console (no run queue): one auditable execution contract and one Stop target, at the cost of not running two projects at once.",\n        "T-02 Page-level rather than component-level specification: stable contracts across refactors, at the cost of implementation freedom inside a page.",\n        "T-03 Approval only for file-write and delegation-launch: no approval fatigue and no route to approve anything dangerous; cost is that a future high-impact action must be classified explicitly (mitigated by non-optional requiresApproval).",\n        "T-04 No free-text workspace path input: eliminates an unvalidated traversal surface; cost is that power users cannot paste a path.",\n        "T-05 Exclusion policy decided in main, user filter only over loaded nodes: one authoritative sandbox, at the cost of filtering not being a whole-workspace search.",\n        "T-06 Read caps surfaced as truncated+counts rather than silently: no partial file is ever presented as complete; cost is more UI states and a deliberately non-saveable truncated buffer.",\n        "T-07 Markdown preview blocks raw HTML and remote images visibly: closes XSS/SSRF/tracking-image vectors; cost is incomplete rendering of some legitimate Markdown.",\n        "T-08 Append-only transcript: the transcript stays an audit artifact; cost is no in-place editing or conversation branching.",\n        "T-09 Settings/History/Audit as overlays, not routes: workspace, run and agent state never restart on navigation; cost is no deep-linking and added overlay-stack management.",\n        "T-10 Agent output as escaped text plus main-generated cards: a prompt injection cannot forge a card or executable UI; cost is no rich presentational answers."\n      ],\n      "enforcement_matrix_highlights": [\n        "Only file.save (when agent-initiated) and delegation.launch carry requiresApproval: true; delegation.launch additionally requires an unexpired approvalId bound to the same toolCallId.",\n        "run.start passes an argv array plus allowlisted env keys — never an interpolated shell string.",\n        "The agent tool vocabulary is the closed union AllowlistedToolName (11 tools incl. the three git_ read-only tools); any other name is refused as tool-not-allowlisted and never dispatched.",\n        "settings.setApiKey is write-only; no interface in the document can read the key back."\n      ],\n      "acceptance_criteria_evidence": {\n        "AC1_every_component_has_an_interface": "Section 17 maps all 24 components to their exported data and action interfaces; the document contains 83 exported interfaces/types.",\n        "AC2_tradeoff_stated_explicitly": "Section 15 states 10 tradeoffs (T-01..T-10), each with the choice, what was gained, what was given up and, where relevant, why it is acceptable.",\n        "other_acs": "Section 18 traces AC-01..AC-21 to the specific page, model field or state that satisfies each; AC-21 is noted as not a UI concern but the interfaces are the typed surface its unit tests assert against."\n      },\n      "open_questions_carried_forward": [\n        "Default delegation CLI: modelled as user-configurable delegationCliLabel with a concrete default chosen at implementation.",\n        "Token-by-token streaming: assumed yes; if buffered, AgentEvent.delta collapses to entry-completed and only the streaming affordance is lost, not the contract.",\n        "In-repo stub model server: assumed under xcoder-dojo/test/; P-05 shows modelState 'error' when unreachable.",\n        "Terminal/SSH/HTTP panels: out of scope (NG-05); P-04 is the only execution surface."\n      ],\n      "observation_for_orchestrator": "The current working root is already named xcoder-dojo-ts (...\\__xcoder__\\xcoder-dojo-ts), while the requirements call for a new sibling folder xcoder-dojo/ inside the workspace. The page specs are path-agnostic, but the implementation stage should confirm which of the two is authoritative before scaffolding, since C-05/data-root and A-04 (no imports from xcoder-ai-dojo/) both depend on that placement."\n    },\n    "files_touched": [\n      ".xcoder/backlog/design-st-2c7624.md"\n    ],\n    "self_check": {\n      "ran": true,\n      "passed": true,\n      "detail": "Extracted all 16 ```ts blocks from the design doc into one compilation unit and ran tsc --strict --noEmit --target ES2022 --module ESNext --moduleResolution bundler. First run failed with a genuine contract gap: contracts.ts(223,25) error TS2304 'Cannot find name MarkdownBlock'. I added the sanitized Markdown AST (MarkdownSpan/MarkdownBlock unions covering paragraph, heading, list, code, image — with raw-HTML and remote-image nodes deliberately absent and counted in a visible `blocked` field), re-extracted and re-ran: EXIT=0, clean under strict. Also verified structure on disk (953 lines, 55,144 bytes, 34 balanced code fences, 20 sections, 0 leftover APPEND-HERE sentinels, 10 tradeoffs, 83 exported interfaces/types). Note: the workspace index excludes dot-directories, so .xcoder/ looks empty to search_workspace/grep/read_file while the file is present on disk — verified via PowerShell. Cleanup: removed the temp check directory and a 