[2026-11-16T09:38:38.122Z] [code-st-1de5aa] [stop=end_turn] [response] Three real findings. Two are wrong test assertions (`hasApiKey` is the *correct* non-secret field), but one is a genuine gap: inline HTML tags inside a paragraph were reaching the AST as literal text. Let me harden the parser.\n\n<action>\n{\n  "tool": "edit_file",\n  "input": {\n    "path": "xcoder-dojo/src/backend/markdown.ts",\n    "old_str": "const HTML_BLOCK = /^\\s*<[a-zA-Z!/][^>]*>/;\nconst IMAGE_MD = /!\\[([^\\]]*)\\]\\(([^)]*)\\)/g;",\n    "new_str": "const HTML_BLOCK = /^\\s*<[a-zA-Z!/][^>]*>/;\nconst HTML_INLINE = /<\\/?[a-zA-Z][^>]*>/g;\nconst IMAGE_MD = /!\\[([^\\]]*)\\]\\(([^)]*)\\)/g;"\n  }\n}\n</action>\n</action>
[2026-11-16T09:38:38.136Z] [code-st-1de5aa] [request] Observation: {"ok":true,"relPath":"xcoder-dojo/src/backend/markdown.ts","replaced":true}
[2026-11-16T09:38:41.026Z] [code-st-1de5aa] [stop=end_turn] [response] Now strip inline HTML tags in the inline parser and count them.\n\n<action>\n{\n  "tool": "edit_file",\n  "input": {\n    "path": "xcoder-dojo/src/backend/markdown.ts",\n    "old_str": "function inline(text: string, counters: Counters): MarkdownSpan[] {\n  const spans: MarkdownSpan[] = [];\n  const replaced = text.replace(IMAGE_MD, (_m, alt: string) => {\n    counters.blockedImages += 1;\n    spans.push({ kind: 'blocked-image', alt });\n    return '';\n  });",\n    "new_str": "function inline(text: string, counters: Counters): MarkdownSpan[] {\n  const spans: MarkdownSpan[] = [];\n  // Inline HTML is stripped before anything else, so a tag can never survive\n  // into a span as literal markup-looking text (design T-07).\n  const withoutHtml = text.replace(HTML_INLINE, () => {\n    counters.strippedHtmlBlocks += 1;\n    return '';\n  });\n  const replaced = withoutHtml.replace(IMAGE_MD, (_m, alt: string) => {\n    counters.blockedImages += 1;\n    spans.push({ kind: 'blocked-image', alt });\n    return '';\n  });"\n  }\n}\n</action>\n</action>
