[2026-11-16T09:55:04.595Z] [test-st-bf6f22] [stop=end_turn] [response] {"thought":"The compound command failed because the shell is cmd.exe, not PowerShell — `Out-Null` and `$d = @'...'@` are not valid there. I have zero turns left, so I cannot patch the harness or re-run. I must report honestly: all 40 assertions pass, but `npm test` never terminates and exits non-zero, so the regression gate (AC3) and therefore AC2 are NOT satisfied. Claiming passed:true would be false. I'll record the defect inline in the deliverable and give the exact reproduction and fix so the next run can apply it.","action":null,"final_answer":{"summary":"Wrote and ran the regression gate. The existing smoke suite (xcoder-dojo/test/smoke.ts, run via `npm test` from the workspace root) executes 40 assertions and ALL 40 pass — but the process never exits and is killed by the timeout, returning exit code 1. So the suite's assertions are green while the gate itself is red. Root cause: the harness never calls process.exit and the async bridge leaves handles alive, so node's event loop never drains. I attempted a fix + RCA write in my final turn, but the command failed because the shell is cmd.exe, not PowerShell (`Out-Null` / `@'...'@` are not valid there) — so neither the patch nor .xcoder/defects/defect0001.md was written. I am reporting this as NOT passed rather than overstating it. NOTE FOR NEXT RUN: there is no vitest in this project (no vitest dependency, no vitest.config.ts); FOLDER_SCOPE's `npx vitest` instruction cannot be executed as specified — the project's real test runner is esbuild+node, which is what I ran.","deliverable":{"suite_run":"npm test  (workspace root -> npm --prefix xcoder-dojo run test -> esbuild test/smoke.ts && node test/smoke.mjs)","verbatim_result":"40 passed, 0 failed","verbatim_process_outcome":"timedOut: true, exitCode: 1 (all 40 assertions PASS; process hangs and is killed)","regression_gate_status":"FAILING (non-zero exit despite 40/40 assertions passing)","pa