rator":["The FOLDER_SCOPE vitest instruction is inapplicable: vitest is not installed and no vitest.config.ts exists. Applying it verbatim would fail with a missing-dependency error, not a test failure.","No src/**/*.test.ts files exist; the project's single suite is test/smoke.ts covering backend+contracts behaviour. UI folders (ui/, main.tsx) have no automated tests at all — coverage gap worth flagging.","Once the exit-guard patch lands, the gate should go green at 40/40 with exit code 0."]},"files_touched":[],"self_check":{"ran":true,"passed":false,"detail":"Ran the full regression gate exactly as the Validation Gate will: `npm test` from the workspace root (delegates to xcoder-dojo). Verbatim output ended with `40 passed, 0 failed` — every one of the 40 assertions passed — but the process did not terminate: tool observation reported `exitCode: 1, timedOut: true`. A non-zero exit plus a hang means AC3 (full regression suite passes independently) is NOT met, and therefore AC2 (self_check.passed) is honestly false. A second command attempting to patch smoke.ts with an exit guard and write .xcoder/defects/defect0001.md failed outright: `'Out-Null' is not recognized as an internal or external command` — the shell is cmd.exe, not PowerShell, so no files were changed and no re-run was possible. Pass count: 40. Fail count: 0 assertions, 1 process-level failure."}}}
